Third-party components and upstream corpora

mbun's own code is licensed under MIT (above). Like Bun, mbun builds against
and ships alongside third-party components; each retains its upstream license:

- WebKit JavaScriptCore (mcpp package mbun.jsc-prebuilt) — LGPL-2.1 and
  BSD-2-Clause, https://webkit.org
- OpenSSL 3 (mbun.openssl) — Apache-2.0, https://www.openssl.org
- mimalloc (mbun.mimalloc) — MIT, https://github.com/microsoft/mimalloc
- SQLite (mbun.sqlite3) — Public Domain, https://sqlite.org
- zlib (mbun.zlib) — zlib license, https://zlib.net
- zstd (mbun.zstd) — BSD-3-Clause / GPL-2.0 dual, https://github.com/facebook/zstd
- brotli (mbun.brotli) — MIT, https://github.com/google/brotli
- libwebp (mbun.libwebp) — BSD-3-Clause, https://chromium.googlesource.com/webm/libwebp

Compatibility inputs pinned as read-only submodules under compat/:

- Bun test and benchmark corpus (compat/bun) — MIT,
  https://github.com/oven-sh/bun
- Node.js test corpus (compat/node) — MIT,
  https://github.com/nodejs/node

Example dependencies installed from npm (Express, Elysia, ...) keep their own
licenses (MIT).
